he's the Commissioner of the National  Hockey League season stopped on March  12th the NHL will now move to a 2014  conference based postseason format that  was approved by the National Hockey  League Players Association last Friday  and the Commissioner joins us now  commissioner thank you for joining us  why did you think going into the  playoffs and that playoff format was the  right move well first of all I want to  know where I can buy that bobblehead of  you playing hockey and I think secondly  and more importantly thanks for having  me and I hope you and all your viewers  and listeners all your colleagues are  well and staying safe you know we have  extraordinary competitive balance our  regular season races to the playoffs go  down to the wires with lots of teams in  contention and if you look at the  standings as of March 12th and we took  the pause there were a lot of clubs on  the bubble and we thought it was only  fair since we couldn't complete the  regular season we were a hundred and  eighty nine games away from completing  the regular season that we had to give  those teams a chance that might very  well have made the playoffs if we had  been able to conclude the regular season  and instead of concluding the regular  season when we came back we were also  mindful of the fact that the players are  gonna have to be away from home and we  didn't want to have that experience to  be prolong any longer than really  necessary I saw we're about 17% of the  NHL our players from outside of North  America what's the biggest concern with  getting them into the state's tested and  you know just the safety precautions  well actually it's seven we have more  probably closer to 25% of our players  are from outside of North America but  17% of our players right now are in  locations outside in what North America  and we have to bring them back obviously  they're there our immigration issues  although since they all have valid visas  that shouldn't be an issue the bigger  issue is is the fact that they were  going to have to quarantine for a couple  of weeks and we're going to when we open  our training facility  which we hope to do the first week of  June they're going to be subject to some  testing as we move to the training camp  phase there'll be more testing and then  when we get to the actual playing test a  playing stage we're being told by our  medical people who were giving us all  the advice on this and whose advice  we're following players if they're not  being tested every day they're going to  be tested at least every other day but  is this the NHL doing the testing or  will it be individual teams doing the  testing well actually it'll be  individual teams in the training camp  and training facilities phase although  we have a backup for clubs that can  arrange to do it locally and any of the  tests we're doing whether it's the  club's the backup or what we're gonna do  when we're actually playing the  competition we're not going to do  anything that would interfere with the  medical needs that may be required for  testing and we're being told by the  experts that by the summer by the summer  there will be such an abundance of  testing our needs will really be  infinitesimal relative to what will be  available could the format of 24 teams  in the playoffs stay after this season  no what we like what we have our regular  season puts teams in the playoffs  virtually all season  we love the way the regular season plays  out it's every games meaningful are our  regular playoffs of 16 teams it's just  the right note the competition is the  entertainment value the excitement the  passion  couldn't be better and so we're doing  something extraordinary in response to  an extraordinary time fans in the stands  any possibility with them you know that  that's something we're not going to have  any control over of it if everything  we're doing is going to be subject to  the guidance and requirements of what  the medical people 