tion that I have to  make properly for another three to four  weeks at that point I'm gonna want to  see a what the state of kovat 19 is in  the communities we're considering  because obviously we reduce the risk of  any of our personal getting in fact that  if we're in place that has very little  Kovan the availability of testing and  the issues relative to moving personnel  across the border either to or from  Canada from the United States so that's  why we didn't want to put all of our  eggs in one basket we think it's better  to have a lot of options so that at the  time we have to make a decision we can  make the best decision possible talking  to the NHL commissioner Gary Bettman I  remember doing an interview with Pete  Rozelle David Stern Peter Ueberroth and  Larry Ziegler and at the time everybody  was commissioners he was the president  when did when did you become a  commissioner instead of the president of  the National Hockey League act actually  in addition to being president as  opposed to Commissioner I think his name  was John now John Ziegler but I think  that might be a golfer Larry Ziegler  when I was hired to come join the NHL  the view was there were lots of things  that needed to be done to modernize the  way the leap was operating at the time  and part of that was part of my  arrangement was I was going to be a  commissioner consistent with what the  other three major leagues were doing as  part of moving the league forward and my  powers got a little increased and it was  really to modernize the structure of how  we were conducting ourselves it sounds  more impressive though I think  Commissioner than president you know it  is what it is it's a word with you know  rose by any other name yes the best  piece of hockey memorabilia you have in  your house is one the best piece of well  I have my plaque from that's nice that's  that's pretty subjective I have before  my six before my 60th birthday I had by  that point my 65th birthday by that  point had presented the cup I don't know  over 20 times and a montage was made up  by Koli Campbell in the hockey  operations department of each of the  pictures of me doing that because the  best thing I get to do is present the  Stanley Cup I give you credit you  you're getting booed but you still love  taking that trophy out there when do I  get booed yeah you know as long as  they're not quiet it's a good thing  there's emotion is passion and hockey  fans are the best hey but you don't want  if you don't have fans this year  commissioner you won't get booed I'd  rather you know what we can pipe it in  how's that  we may do that Commissioner thank you  for joining us good luck with the  proposal in the format we appreciate  your time  thanks for having me I hope you your  family thank you that's the Commissioner  of the National Hockey League Gary  Bettman

